  "id": "information-processing",
  "term": "information processing",
  "definition": "In psychology, information processing can refer to the mental handling of cues or information that helps a person form an appropriate response. In the social context described here, problems processing social cues can make it harder for children to choose suitable behavior in everyday situations.",
